@h1 Composing constructs h1@

Once you know each primitive, the interesting question is how they stack: data
feeding iteration feeding conditionals, captures fed by data access, definitions
that use other definitions. This short bridge page shows the happy seams — and
the two places where constructs intentionally do @strong not strong@ compose, so
you meet the errors before they surprise you.

@h2 Data, iteration, and conditionals together h2@

The workhorse pattern — loop a collection of records, gate each with a condition:

@@@pre
#hands: [ { name - Ada, awake - true }, { name - Bo, awake - false } ]

(each @hands as hand)
  (if @hand.awake is true) @hand.name is on watch. (end)
(end)
pre@@@

(fixture 17-combinations/record-iteration-conditional.) Data access works as a
parameter value (access-in-param) and as a condition's left-hand side
(access-in-condition).

@h2 Captures fed by data h2@

A definition's captures can be filled from a data record read with dotted
access:

@@@pre
#weil: { author - Simone Weil, work - Gravity and Grace }

#cite ||author, work|| ::author::, _::work::_. cite#

@cite |author @weil.author| |work @weil.work| cite@
pre@@@

(fixture definition-with-captures-and-data.) A definition body may reference
another definition (def-of-def), and inline emphasis composes inside a block
body:

@@@pre
@aside She _crossed_ the *threshold* at dusk. aside@
pre@@@

(emphasis-inside-node-body.)

@h2 The seams that do not compose h2@

@strong Seam 1 — @@@code !! code@@@ is not a use-side closer. strong@ The
@@@code !! code@@@ token closes a value-block @em definition em@; it does not
short-close a node @em use em@. So an inner node left open inside a body is never
closed by @@@code !! code@@@ and you get @code E_UNCLOSED_NODE code@ (fixture
nested-nodes-with-params). Close inner nodes with their own
@@@code name@ code@@@.

@strong Seam 2 — an injected node still needs its closer. strong@ A bare
@@@code @inset code@@@ on its own line opens a block that expects
@@@code inset@ code@@@; if the surrounding body closes first, it hits the wrong
closer — @code E_MISMATCHED_CLOSE code@ (fixture
script-injects-rendered-content). A script that injects rendered content must
supply balanced open/close, not a half-open node.

@h2 Common mistakes h2@

@ul
@li Using @@@code !! code@@@ to close a node use — it closes a value-block
definition only. li@
@li Expecting a script-injected node to auto-close — supply its
@@@code name@ code@@@. li@
ul@

